<title>SWEDEN: Avesta Sheffield plunges into loss.</title>
<headline>Avesta Sheffield plunges into loss.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to December 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					   (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Result after fin items	LOSS  136     vs  3,146 PROFIT</p>
<p> Turnover			     12,646     vs 16,602</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)			LOSS 0.24   vs     13.70 PROFIT</p>
<p> Operating profit			224     vs  3,433</p>
<p> Depreciation			    377     vs    369</p>
<p> Interests in associate companies    6     vs     78</p>
<p> Net financial items		    11     vs	4</p>
<p> Tax				CREDIT  88     vs    962</p>
<p> Minorities		     CREDIT  10     vs     19  CHARGE</p>
<p> Net result			 LOSS  38     vs  2,165  PROFIT</p>
<p>NOTE -- Analysts expected Avesta Sheffield to post a pre-tax profit of 163 million crowns for the first nine months of 1996/97.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
